course: dictionary
lesson: 14343
title: Odes: poems of praise
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An ode is a poem that praises someone or something. The poet speaks to it directly, often in a grand, serious style, as if it can hear.
explain: Poets have written odes for centuries. Keats wrote «To Autumn» and «Ode to a Nightingale», and you may read them in English lessons. Each one celebrates something: the season, or a bird's song.
explain: The word can be playful too. «An ode to pizza» is a fun way to say you are celebrating pizza, even if no one writes a long poem. Look for the phrase «an ode to»: the words after it tell you what is being praised.
fact: An ode is a noun. One is an ode, and more than one are odes.
fact: An ode is a poem that praises or speaks to someone or something.
fact: «Ode to Joy» is a famous tune by Beethoven, from his Ninth Symphony.
fact: Today «Ode to Joy» is the anthem of Europe.
fact: The phrase «an ode to» shows what is being celebrated, as in «an ode to the sea».
exercise: «The poet wrote an ode to the sea.» What is an ode in this sentence? | A ship that sails across the sea | A kind of seaweed | *A poem that praises the sea | A map of the coast
exercise: In «an ode to pizza», what is being celebrated? | A plate | *Pizza | A table | A chef
exercise: Which composer wrote the famous tune «Ode to Joy»? | *Beethoven | Bach | Elgar | Mozart
test: «She wrote an ode to her dog, praising every wag of his tail.» What is the poet doing? | Giving a warning | Telling a sad story | Selling a pet | *Praising her dog
test: What does the phrase «an ode to» tell you? | *What is being praised or celebrated | How long a poem is | Where a poem was written | A question someone is asking
exam: Which statement about an ode is true? | An ode is a question about the weather | An ode is a poem that praises someone or something | *An ode is a poem that praises someone or something, and it is always a noun in a sentence | An ode is a kind of bird
